{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ORCHESTRATION MODEL + WAVE PLAN (2026-09-03) — resumed under corrected execution model.\n\nMain session = ORCHESTRATOR only. Each leaf ticket is delegated to its own background agent\nthat owns it end-to-end (fresh worktree off origin/main -> plan-review -> claim -> held-out TDD\n(the leaf agent runs the hold-out internally, dispatching its own implementer sub-agent) ->\nlocal gates -> Gerrit push -> land at LLM-Review+1 & Verified+1 -> completion-verifier + AC\nboxes -> close). Shared discipline: session files/leaf-execution-protocol.md. Agents MUST NOT\nforce; blockers are surfaced to the orchestrator.\n\nOperator decisions recorded: Decision A (config-alias removal) APPROVED — clean removal, NOT\nfail-loud tombstones (see 038d comment). Decision B (no internal-only shims) APPROVED (see 6640\ncomment).\n\nWAVE 1 (dispatched now, mutually file-disjoint, parallel):\n- 8eff  ADR: prohibit internal-only shims (Decision B; critical path, unblocks a691/3a46/2164/e54e)\n- 828b  Remove three scheduled public deprecations (resume claimed)\n- 21de  Git-backed module-size trend metrics\n- 38ab  Conflict-safe reconciliation sidecar persistence\n- aa9e  Pinned Semgrep/Gitleaks in Verified\n- b35a  Generate ticket taxonomy docs from schema (plan rewrite first)\n\nSERIALIZED / HELD:\n- 8ca7 (ADR-A) after 8eff lands (docs/adr overlap), then unblocks 7370 -> 1a63.\n- f773 after 828b lands (CHANGELOG + CLI overlap).\n- a691/3a46/2164/e54e unblock after 8eff lands.\n- Reconcile family 0cfc/82bb/c195 held (overlaps 38ab reconciler files)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788468385481487850,"uuid":"09ebbd61-88bd-49a1-8448-6fca237cfc60"}